SMP out of the box: banked GICC frame default + clear SIGPdisabled by default.

Hardware-controlled A/B (kernel run 44727048801, cmdline only) finally solved
the multi-year self-IPI problem:

  sweetgiccoff=0x2000 (old default, per-CPU frames) -> cpus=4 dies before
      any log;  sweetgiccoff=0 + sweetsgidbg=1 -> CPU1 runs to mark=7 but
      "NOT alive after 5s, sig=0, sig_raw=0x80000000";
  sweetgiccoff=0 + sweetsgidbg=2 -> SUCCESS:
      cpu0/1/2/3 all "came alive; SGI1 OK",
      "4/4 CPUs initialized, SGI1 verified (dropped=0)",
      stable 17 min to sweetrebootat=960, reached launchd, log flush #80.

Two facts, now made the kernel DEFAULT so no sweet* boot args are needed:

1. pe_fiq.c: gicc_stride default 0x2000 -> 0.  The GIC-400 CPU-interface
   registers are banked at ONE physical address (hardware selects the bank by
   the current PE); 0153's "0x2000 apart per CPU" assumption was wrong.  The
   sweetgiccoff/sweetgiccbase overrides remain for A/B.

2. SweetCPU.cpp: SIGPdisabled is cleared directly at the end of initCPU by
   default.  The self-IPI handler (cpu_signal_handler_internal) never clears
   it on this GIC-400, so a real SGI1 does not complete the handshake.  New
   boot arg `sweetclearsigp` defaults to 1 (= clear, working); =0 restores
   the old pure-IPI behaviour for A/B.  The sweetsgidbg>=2 fallback stays.

Verified baseline: xnu buildtree of run 44727048801 (through 0159).
Next patch number: 0161.
--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c
@@ -252,7 +252,7 @@
 static vm_offset_t gicd_base;
 static vm_offset_t gicc_base;      /* CPU0's frame (or sweetgiccbase override) */
 static vm_offset_t gicc_this;      /* this PE's CPU-interface frame (0153) */
-static uint32_t gicc_stride = 0x2000;  /* GIC-400: per-CPU GICC frame stride */
+static uint32_t gicc_stride = 0;  /* 0160: GICC frames are banked; all PEs share one frame */
 
 static uint32_t
 gic_read32(vm_offset_t addr)
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
@@ -798,6 +798,32 @@
 				    sweet_cpu_get_signal_raw(getCPUNumber()));
 			}
 		}
+		/*
+		 * 0160: make the successful SMP handshake the DEFAULT, no longer
+		 * dependent on `sweetsgidbg=2`.  Controlled A/B on hardware:
+		 *   sweetgiccoff=0 + sweetsgidbg=1 -> CPU1 NOT alive, sig=0;
+		 *   sweetgiccoff=0 + sweetsgidbg=2 -> 4/4 CPUs initialized,
+		 *     stable to sweetrebootat.  The self-IPI handler never clears
+		 *     SIGPdisabled on this GIC-400, so the handshake must clear it
+		 *     directly.  Default ON; sweetclearsigp=0 restores the pure-IPI
+		 *     behaviour for A/B.  gicc_stride now defaults to 0 (banked
+		 *     frame) in pe_fiq.c, together making cpus=4 work out of the box.
+		 */
+		{
+			uint32_t clearsigp = 1;
+
+			if (PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetclearsigp", &clearsigp,
+			    sizeof(clearsigp)) == 0) {
+				clearsigp = 1;	/* default ON */
+			}
+			if (clearsigp != 0) {
+				sweet_cpu_sigpdisabled_clear();
+				kprintf("SWEET CPU: cpu=%u cleared SIGPdisabled "
+				    "(0160 default, sig=0x%08x)\n",
+				    getCPUNumber(),
+				    sweet_cpu_get_signal_raw(getCPUNumber()));
+			}
+		}
 	}
 	/* 0142: mark 6 - self-IPI queued. */
 	sweet_smp_mark(getCPUNumber(), 6);
